  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x+12\\ge 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-7x+12\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/5423f579b521506be23a372cb13f2e2c6593e1efd822600f153d76a94fef86ce.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le 3$ or $x\\ge 4.$",
